    "Gamified HP / damage / intercept catalogue for OASIS. All numbers are PUBLIC ESTIMATES or archetype tuning values, not performance data. Deterministic: every random draw is a seeded Bernoulli (see research/damage-model.md).",
    "id matches mirrorworld/catalog.py type where one exists; `aliases` lists the asset_cat branch ids (data/assets.json) so both catalogues resolve to the same item.",
    "hp: abstract hit points. armor: 0-1 fractional damage reduction. damage.payload_hp: damage at ground zero; damage.blast_radius_m: falloff to 0. damage.warhead_kg: public estimate the payload_hp is scaled from (roughly payload_hp ~= 18 * kg, sub-linear for large warheads).",
    "defenders: p_kill is per engagement window (default window_s=10) while target is inside engage_range_m; each window consumes 1 ammo; reload_s after ammo runs out. A successful engagement applies damage_on_hit (>= hp of the intended target class = a kill).",
    "Realism caps: max_concurrent_targets on defenders, ammo limits, and scenario-level limits (max 12 attackers per 10x10 km tile) keep fights plausible."
  ],
